      "created_at": "2015-01-13T18:23:16.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hey everyone.</p><p><span>Before I start,&nbsp;firstly I just wanna introduce myself (being new n' all).&nbsp;</span><span>I only found out about Sentinels of the Mutliverse a few days ago via Steam. When I saw it I thought to my self \"What the heck, it looks fun - I'm gonna buy it\" - so I did. And oh man, I have had so much fun. I love the game, the characters - all of it. In fact, Sentinels is the only game that I enjoyed so much to actually wright a (positive :D) Steam review for. So a big thanks to Christopher (and the devs) for making such an awesome game.</span></p><p>And since I have been enjoying SotM so much, I want to talk and socialise with others who enjoy and play the game! That is why I firstly came here to the forum - but I have also been hanging out in the Steam group chat for SotM for two days now - and it has been completely empty. *sadface*</p><p>So I am wondering if anyone else here uses/would use the Steam chat? I know there is no technical multiplayer in the game right now, but I just thought it would be nice if the community could have a place to meet and chat, other than just the forums. That is also why I mention Teamspeak in the topic title. I know some have used Skype to play SotM (digital version) together/socialise and talk about SotM, but Skype isn't a collective room that people can join and leave, such as teamspeak is.</p><p>So I was wondering 1. If anyone would like to use the Steam chat for SotM as a social zone for players, and 2. If an official SotM Teamspeak 3 server would be a possiblility (such a server would be of huge benefit especially for when multiplayer goes live for the Steam version).</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thanks all. :)</p>",
