      "id": 127134,
      "name": "Ameena",
      "username": "Ameena",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-13T22:05:45.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Skype doesn't have to have video…I mean, it <span class=\"bbcode-i\">can</span>, but I've never personally used it (though I've chatted to my sister when she was working in Egypt and had a webcam). I just text chat to people, generally, except for my partner whom I voice chat with every night (well, nearly - tonight is an extremely rare exception as he's working a night shift and would've already left for that by the time I got home from work :(), because he's not very fast at typing and also because we game together a lot and voice chat makes things so much easier :).</p>\n<p>I did have Teamspeak on my old computer when I was part of a gaming group but only used it a couple of times.</p>\n<p>I didn't know Steam had actual multiple-person chat. So far I've only ever used it to chat to the very few people in my friends list. I'm not even sure if it has audio chat (but probably - most such chat features seem to have audio now, though I'm not fussed about using it unless I'm gaming with someone).</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:01:41.972Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
