      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/nuukov/{size}/2576_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-13T22:53:01.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>@Pydro - Thanks!</p><p>@Ameena - Yeah, well Skype is more useful for general communication (calling and video calls), while Teamspeak is more orientated for communities and gaming (eats up less RAM IIRC). But yeah, on Steam if you go to the Sentinels of the Multiverse: The Video Game Community Hub, in the top right it will say \"X&nbsp;in Group Chat\" - \"Group Chat\" will be underlined and if you click on it, it will connect you to that group chat. There is also a group voice chat system apparently, but it most likely sucks. (This is where Teamspeak would be more useful).</p>",
